Reading the staged context files to propose plan-review archetypes.
Checking repo evidence against the plan to identify gaps the static panel might miss.
{"archetypes":[{"name":"security-merge-trim","focus_area":"risk-integration","weight":1,"rationale":"The plan targets a single stale emergency/merge sentence inside one dense SECURITY.md paragraph; verify the edit removes the mutual-exclusion and automated-merge consequence clauses without disturbing adjacent admission-gate or bypass wording.","prompt_body":"Compare the planned SECURITY.md edit against the live Preflight admission paragraph and confirm the obsolete mutually-exclusive and cannot-merge consequence text is fully removed. Check that no remaining sentence still implies emergency runs cannot reach automated merge paths or reintroduces admission suppression. Verify the replacement compatibility sentence matches current /implement --emergency and --merge behavior in skills/implement and python/admission.py. Flag any plan step that broadens the edit into gate-list, bypass-scope, or unrelated emergency downgrade bullets beyond the approved outline. Cite specific file paths and line ranges for any issues found, and follow the output-format rules from your outer wrapper exactly."},{"name":"relevant-checks-surface","focus_area":"correctness","weight":1,"rationale":"No implement-preflight route exists in relevant-checks.sh today; the plan must add a four-file case block beside implement-finalize without breaking the multi-case loop pattern or omitting the harness markdown sibling.","prompt_body":"Inspect run_direct_relevant_targets in scripts/relevant-checks.sh and verify the plan names the correct insertion site adjacent to the existing implement-finalize route. Confirm all four scoped paths (implement-preflight.sh, implement-preflight.md, test-implement-preflight.sh, test-implement-preflight.md) map to the existing Makefile target test-implement-preflight and that append_target_once dedupes correctly. Check the plan does not add Python lint or pytest targets for this offline Bash harness surface. Flag missing routes, wrong target names, or placement that splits related implement helper surfaces across distant case blocks. Cite specific file paths and line ranges for any issues found, and follow the output-format rules from your outer wrapper exactly."},{"name":"refusal-first-line-kv","focus_area":"correctness","weight":1,"rationale":"Four admission-block harness cases still use broad contains checks while the plan adds exact first-line templates that must match print_admission_refusal output byte-for-byte including backticks and ADMISSION_RESULT tokens.","prompt_body":"Cross-check each planned first-line refusal string against scripts/implement-preflight.sh print_admission_refusal and the existing managed-prefix first-line assertion pattern in scripts/test-implement-preflight.sh. Verify ADMISSION_RESULT token names (has-blockers, missing-designed-prefix, report-title) and the ADMISSION_ERROR=gh=down branch match stub output ordering so sed -n 1p compares the true first stdout line. Confirm secondary contains assertions for BLOCKERS= and TITLE= remain on later lines and are not displaced by the new checks. Flag template drift, wrong branch ordering for admission-error, or assertions that would pass if a warning line precedes the refusal. Cite specific file paths and line ranges for any issues found, and follow the output-format rules from your outer wrapper exactly."}]}
